 "text": "Hello there, how's your day? Roughly in the middle of area, and well away from any entrances so it' easy to find. You want it to be out of direct wind too, so cold air doesn't stream in. That's a great spot if you can get permission from the landowner. tent will be out of sight, which is important for some people, and it' well protected from wind. You can spruce it up with some new anchor cords and some fresh window mesh if you like. Or you could move it onto a balconies tent. Keep a tent between it and the site if you' using one night after dark, and check with your headtorch first if you' unsure. Flat is the way to go, it's much harder to blow over. Just stake it off the car boot and the tent door, and keep one entrance hole small while it's windy.",
